# ==== T-FMT-D (R41) fill-pack matrix — LIST KIND = CLOSURE-PARAMETER list.
#
# SUBJECT: this fixture asserts `gg fmt` OUTPUT (byte-for-byte, in
# `fmt_fill_pack_closure_params_kind`) — a bulk `gg fmt` sweep MUST EXCLUDE it.
#
# Emit site: the `Expr::Closure` arm of `format_expr` -> the delimited-list
# chokepoint `emit_delimited_list("(", ")", ..)` -> `doc::surround_fill`.
#
# Axis cell claim (Core #12 — `list kind x fit` for the CLOSURE-PARAM kind ONLY):
#   cl_empty  empty              `()` — the zero-parameter closure
#   cl_flat   fits-flat          one line, no trailing comma
#   cl_fill   needs-fill         greedy packing at the block continuation indent
#   cl_over   suffix-over-width  the one closure parameter does not fit on the open
#                                line, so it breaks to the continuation indent —
#                                where it FITS ALONE at 119 columns. The line
#                                reaches 122 because of the `): 0` its CALLER
#                                writes after the close.
#
# ⚠ cl_over is NOT an unbreakable atom, and this header used to say it was
# ("being wider than the budget it overflows even there" — contradicted by the
# NOTE two paragraphs down, which named the caller suffix as the cause). It is
# A8's INLINE-BODY CLOSURE escape: the parameter list has already broken as far
# as it can, the element sits alone at the minimum column with no interior break
# opportunity of its own, and the inline body still rides the same line. Widening
# "atom" to cover it would swallow the whole caller-suffix class — the exact
# class the tail reserve exists to close.
#
# The `: <body>` tail is NO LONGER invisible to the packer: R42 carries it into
# the fit test as `doc::Renderer::tail_reserve`, which is why the OTHER rows here
# are now decided with their suffix counted. cl_over is what remains after that:
# the reserve is charged correctly and no break can spend it.
#
# RED source per row: cl_fill / cl_over are TRUE pre-fix REDs (one closure
# parameter per line with a trailing comma, and `): body` hanging off a bare `)`
# line). cl_empty / cl_flat are invariant — break-and-restore them by lowering
# `doc::MAX_WIDTH`.
void cl_empty():
    auto e = (): 0

void cl_flat():
    auto f = (int aaaa, int bbbb, int cccc): aaaa

void cl_fill():
    auto g = (int aaaaaaaa, int bbbbbbbb, int cccccccc, int dddddddd, int eeeeeeee, int ffffffff, int gggggggg, int hhhhhhhh): aaaaaaaa

void cl_over():
    auto h = (VeryLongClosureParameterTypeNameForTheOverWidthCell aSingleClosureParameterWhoseWidthExceedsTheWholeLineBudget): 0
